course: dictionary
lesson: 10125
title: Thoughtless words and actions
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Thoughtless means not thinking about how your actions or words affect other people. It is often unkind or rude, but it can also mean careless: done without thinking about what might happen. Look at the words around it to see which meaning fits.
explain: «Just a pig—a plain pig!» Here pig does not mean an animal on a farm. The speaker is calling someone a pig, which means a selfish, thoughtless person who does not think about others. The context shows this, because the words are an insult.
explain: Try the swap test. Put «a careless remark» in place of «a thoughtless remark» and see if the meaning still fits. Phrases like «how thoughtless of me» show that the speaker has realised they forgot to think about someone else.
explain: A thoughtless remark can hurt someone's feelings even if it was not meant badly. A thoughtless action, like leaving a toy on the stairs, can cause an accident. Thoughtful people think before they act or speak.
fact: Thoughtless is an adjective: thoughtless, more thoughtless, most thoughtless.
fact: «Thoughtless» means not thinking about how your actions or words affect other people.
fact: «Thoughtless» can also mean careless: done without thinking about what might happen.
fact: «A thoughtless remark» can hurt someone's feelings even if it was not meant badly.
fact: «How thoughtless of me!» is what you say when you realise you have forgotten or hurt someone.
exercise: «Just a pig—a plain pig!» Here pig means what? | A very clean pet | *A selfish, thoughtless person | A type of hot dinner | A farm animal with muddy feet
exercise: Sam forgot Ali's birthday and said, «How thoughtless of me!» What does thoughtless mean here? | Thinking very hard about a sum | Quick and clever | Full of happy thoughts | *Not thinking about how forgetting would affect Ali
exercise: Which action is thoughtless? | Saying thank you for a gift | *Leaving a toy on the top step, where someone could trip over it | Putting your coat on the peg | Helping a friend carry the bags
test: Which word means the same as thoughtless in the sense of careless? | *Careless | Thankful | Careful | Thoughtful
test: The speaker said, «a thoughtless remark», about a joke that upset a friend. What does thoughtless tell us? | The speaker was sorry for a very long time | *The speaker did not think how the joke would hurt the friend | The speaker thought carefully about how the joke would feel | The friend was being thoughtless
exam: Which sentence uses thoughtless correctly? | Thoughtless means bouncy and cheerful | *Leaving your bike in the doorway, without a thought for others, was thoughtless | Thoughtless is a kind of cake | The thoughtless sun rose over the hill
